I tend to go hot and cold on Nethack, so Punc's early adventures are lost
forever in the mists of time. Still using 3.4.1. Not much stands out now.
Found Ludios. Nalzak was a pushover. No sign of Demogorgon. I think I had
to wish for gauntlets of dexterity. Had a pet pyrolisk for a while, but I
got tired to lugging him along, and left him behind to become peaceful.
Never did see or get an artifact weapon, apart from Sting, and finished the
game with a ordinary mace. Is there a good artifact weapon for Priest/esses
to use?

 I got to the edge of the final push and put off doing it for a long while,
mostly because I was afraid Punc wasn't up to the challenge; the RNG had
been rather stingy when it came to doling out both spellbooks and magic
markers. (I personally don't like to engage in polypiling) I finally burned
a wish or two to bulk up my AC and took the plunge. it turned out Punc
*was* up to it, but it was a near thing a couple of times. Had to keep
quaffing potions of full healing as she was mobbed by Wizard "pets" and
Lich-summoned monsters. The Temple was a grinding slog; I had two
arch-liches tag-teaming me and porting in swarms and swarms of monsters. I
finally got fed up and wished for a scroll of genocide and got rid of all
liches. (An earlier throne let me get rid of MMFs as well.)  Used a
cockatrice corpse to carve a path of destruction through the survivors, and
then blasted my way into the Temple with liberal use of a wand of death.
Killed the (doubled) Wizard and the High Priest and got the Amulet. The
High Priest was carrying the first and only spellbook of Extra Healing that
I came across in the entire game. (The RNG cheerfully gave me Finger of
Death, but Healing? Nooo. I finished the game with my Healing ability still
Unskilled.) Since Punc was chaotic, the trip back up topside was relatively
pain-free, with only a few more attacks from the Wizard along the way. Used
her crystal ball to blast her way quickly through the elemental planes.
Almost got nailed by an air elemental when I stupidly tried to cut through
the clouds in Air. Lost useful rings to an electric eel attack on Water.
Not a single Archon sighted anywhere, for which I was extremely grateful.
Never invoked the Mitre.
  Got lucky on the Astral plane. Chopped down Death after he sucked a
couple levels out of me, waded through the usual sea of monsters, and the
first altar I visited was the correct one. If I had had to fight my way
back across the level I might have been in trouble; there was such a mob I
had to kick down the door just to get to the altar, and there was a horde
of angry angels on my tail. Anyway, off to heaven...

